--- body ---
## Context
Author request, 2026-11-01. Bring the CIRED archives into the RAG's
collection, next to the HAL publications. They are inventoried by the
author's project archiveCIRED (github.com/MinhHaDuong/archiveCIRED, "Inventaire
et archivage de la production scientifique du CIRED (1970-2013)"): about 1112
logical documents over 1991 files (doc_index.json over file_index.json),
catalogued in a private Zotero group. That project chose a private group to
avoid triaging rights document by document, and matches records by
identifier, never by title (titles repeat across distinct works).

## Questions to settle first
- Rights: which documents may be indexed and quoted; the archives were kept
  private for a reason. Ticket 0013 (internal CIRED service, no public
  access) changes what is acceptable; decide with it.
- Source and format: export from archiveCIRED's index or its Zotero group
  (metadata plus PDF), how many have usable text (scans need OCR).
- Identity: dedupe against HAL by identifier (HAL id, DOI, Zotero key),
  never by title; mark provenance so answers say "CIRED archives" vs "HAL".
- Delivery between projects: archiveCIRED provides the export through its own
  tickets/ (cross-project rule: a ticket there, never an edit from here).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Rights decision recorded (which subset, internal-only or public), with ticket 0013
- [ ] A companion ticket filed in archiveCIRED for the export, and the export received
- [ ] Archive documents ingested with provenance metadata; OCR where needed; no duplicate of a HAL record (identifier match)
- [ ] Answers cite archive documents distinctly from HAL; a test query on a known pre-2000 archive document finds it
